# Maintainer tooling output
.pytest_cache/

# Credentials — never in a repository. The only place a token lives on this
# machine is ~/.aion/api_tokens.json, outside every working tree, and the only
# way one reaches a command is through an environment variable at the moment it
# is needed. A token in a repo survives every later attempt to delete it,
# because git keeps history.
api_tokens.json
api_tokens.json.bak*
*.pat
*_token.json
*_tokens.json
*credentials*.json
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.local.example
.netrc
*.pem
*.key
!**/public*.key

# ingest/ and data/ moved to AION-Analytics-India/aion-market-calendar-data in
# 1.0.0. One manifest schema means one ingestion tool maintains both calendars;
# two copies would drift, which is how these packages ended up with different
# update mechanisms in the first place.
